Ghosts at least are visually indistinguishable from
solid rock, and have been "since forever". I can't
comment on "shades", I haven't played the ASCII
version that deep in the dungeons.

Doing a bit of source diving, all refs to 3.4.3,
unpatched vanilla.

In monst.c line 42, we learn that the last entry in
the monster data structure is the foreground color:

 *	symbol color (C(x) macro)

While at line 2522 we learn that the symbol color is
CLR_GRAY for ghosts:

	M2_NOPOLY|M2_UNDEAD|M2_STALK|M2_HOSTILE, M3_INFRAVISION, CLR_GRAY),

And at line 2531 we learn that the symbol color is
CLR_BLACK for shades:

	M3_INFRAVISION, CLR_BLACK),

